{
  "version": "2.17",
  "children": [
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "Zb3v5",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "name": "Brief · Reglas y avisos",
      "width": 360,
      "fill": "$bg-muted",
      "cornerRadius": "$radius-md",
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": "$space-4",
      "padding": "$space-5",
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "sOker",
          "name": "BT",
          "fill": "$fg-default",
          "content": "BRIEF — Reglas y avisos · happy path",
          "fontFamily": "$font-display",
          "fontSize": 18,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "hBhm5",
          "name": "BB",
          "fill": "$fg-subtle",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "kit-version-source: 1.0.0 · updated: 2026-09-16\n\n1. PURPOSE\nThe Reglas tab and the inbox behind the bell: the rules the owner defines, and everything the app decides to tell him. One file, because rules are one of four notification producers and the bandeja is where all four land.\n\n2. ENTRY POINTS\n- Reglas — BottomNav tab (/alerts, alerts#index)\n- Nueva regla — \"Nueva\" opens /alerts/new inside a <dialog> (D11, components/_sheet_dialog); a suggestion's \"Crear\" pre-fills it\n- Bandeja — the TopBar bell and \"Ver bandeja\" (/notifications)\n\n3. SCREENS (left → right)\n- Reglas · Vacío — no rules yet: KPIs at zero, suggestions from what is held, an empty feed\n- Nueva regla · Sheet — a price cross, the default chip\n- Nueva regla · Calendario — a marketwide date rule: no asset, no threshold, \"Días antes\"\n- Reglas · Default — rules, últimos disparos, cómo te aviso\n- Bandeja · Default — one group per day (D119)\n- Bandeja · Vacía\n\n4. BUSINESS RULES\n- A field shows only where the contract reads it: date rules take window_days, never a threshold; bmv_holiday and cete_auction have no asset (alerts/contracts/create_contract.rb)\n- Thresholds are inclusive — the evaluator compares with >= and <= (alerts/domain/alert_evaluator.rb) — so the copy says \"o más\" and \"o menos\"\n- Volume is compared against AlertEvaluator::VOLUME_AVERAGE_DAYS, five days\n- A day-change notice carries the measured move with its sign (D119)\n- Up to three suggestions, derived from holdings, never one already created (alerts/domain/rule_suggestions.rb)\n- The bandeja is not a channel you toggle. Cómo te aviso switches the daily digest, urgent email and push; push renders only when VAPID keys exist\n- Nothing on these screens tells the owner what to do (ADR-001)\n\n5. COPY SOURCE\nconfig/locales/es-MX.yml — alerts.*, notifications.*, notificaciones.*, settings.show (the switches). Notices: Alerts::Domain::TriggerNotice, Trading::UseCases::NotifyApproachingEarnings and NotifyApproachingMaturities, ResolveTrackedSymbolsJob, CheckSyncHealthJob. Rule summaries: AlertsHelper.\n\n6. STATES NOT DRAWN\n- Bandeja with a filter that matches nothing — the empty card reads \"Nada en este filtro. Prueba otro.\"\n- Reglas · Vacío with no holdings — the suggestions block and \"Crear una desde cero\" are absent\n- Nueva regla on the other conditions — the threshold label reads \"Cambio en el día · %\", \"Nivel RSI\" or \"Múltiplo del promedio\"\n- Nueva regla on a phone — the sheet caps at 85% of the viewport and scrolls; the artboards draw it whole\n- The empty-state card's dashed border — the .pen format has no dashed stroke\n- Desktop — D4: the list and the sheet reflow\n\n7. OPEN FINDINGS\nNone.\n\n8. HISTORY\n→ Log frame, below this brief. Reasoning before 2026-09-16: git show 120600bb:design/V2_REMAINING.md (ALR-*).",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "$font-sans",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
